# TestedBiomarkerTeam rules — `tested_biomarker_umbrella`

This section answers "**what was tested**" — the full panel of genes/biomarkers
that were assayed, whether or not a variant was found. Emit the umbrella object
with `count_of_tested_biomarkers`, `page_numbers` (pages where the panel grid
appears), `llm_confidence_score`, and `tested_biomarkers` (a flat, deduplicated,
**alphabetized** array of strings).

## 1. What to include

- Every gene / biomarker named as part of the panel, analysis, or coverage list
  — even when its result is "no variant detected" or it never appears again.
- This is the broadest recall surface in the document: panel grids, "genes
  analyzed" appendices, coverage tables, methodology gene lists. Read them all
  (recall mandate) — the parser hypothesis seed will undercount panel lists.

## 2. What to EXCLUDE

- **Testing methods are not biomarkers.** Never list `NGS`, `MSI` (as a method),
  `FISH`, `IHC`, `Sanger`, `PCR`, `Sequencing` as panel members.
- Non-gene QC/coverage rows (e.g. "mean coverage", "tumor purity") are not
  tested biomarkers.
- Do not duplicate a gene that appears in both a results table and the panel
  appendix — `tested_biomarkers` is a **set**.

## 3. Normalization + dedup

- **List the GENE, not the specific variant.** The panel entry is the gene that
  was tested — `JAK2`, not `JAK2 V617F`; `BRAF`, not `BRAF V600E`. Strip the
  variant/mutation suffix to the bare gene symbol. So a "JAK2 V617F Mutation
  Analysis" contributes exactly one panel entry: `JAK2`.
- Use HGNC-preferred symbols where applicable (call `hgnc_normalize` if it's in
  your tool list). After normalization, dedup case-insensitively, then sort
  alphabetically (A→Z) for a stable, comparable list.
- A biomarker tested under an alias and its canonical form collapse to one entry
  (HER2/ERBB2 → `ERBB2`); a gene and its variant collapse to the gene
  (`JAK2` + `JAK2 V617F` → `JAK2`).

## 4. `count_of_tested_biomarkers` and `page_numbers`

- `count_of_tested_biomarkers` = length of the deduped `tested_biomarkers` array.
- `page_numbers` = DERIVED sorted list of the pages where the panel/grid appears
  (from tool-result blocks).

## 4b. `biomarkers_tested_no_result` — tested but NO definitive result

Production-parity. Separate from `tested_biomarkers` (which is the with-result
panel), capture biomarkers that were **tested but returned no definitive
result**, each as an object `{name, reason, details}`:
- `name` — the biomarker/gene (NOT a method).
- `reason` — why no result: `"QNS"` (quantity not sufficient), `"Pending"`,
  `"Indeterminate"`, `"Equivocal"`, `"Not reported"`.
- `details` — any extra note, else null.
Emit `[]` when every tested biomarker has a result (the JAK2 demo → `[]`).

**Mutually exclusive — a biomarker belongs to exactly ONE list.** If a
biomarker yielded no usable result (QNS / Pending / Indeterminate / Equivocal /
Not reported), it goes in `biomarkers_tested_no_result` and must NOT also appear
in `tested_biomarkers`. `tested_biomarkers` is the with-result panel only. Note
the boundary: "negative" / "not detected" / "no variant" / "wild type" IS a
definitive result → `tested_biomarkers`; only the absence of a result (the
reasons above) routes a biomarker to `biomarkers_tested_no_result`.

## 5. `llm_confidence_score`

Top-level float in [0.0, 1.0] for the section. A panel grid read cleanly →
0.9+; a list reconstructed from scattered methodology prose → lower.

---

Now run the ReAct loop and produce the `tested_biomarker_umbrella` object with a
deduplicated, alphabetized `tested_biomarkers` array.
